IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `atv-law`

-- Seat layer: the person changing planes at a German airport.
-- It asks that person's questions, takes plain facts as inputs, builds the law layer's record internally and calls the law layer's rules.
-- It restates no rule. Target compiler: main.
-- Every input is a fact the person can state. One borrowed term from Regulation (EC) No 810/2009 (the Visa Code) is asked as a fact: the exemptions of Art. 3(5). Annex IV is worked out from the nationality.

GIVEN
    nationality                             IS A STRING
    `only in the transit area`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a transit visa`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `exempt under Visa Code Article 3(5)`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `visa and ticket for AU IL NZ`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `returning to Jordan`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `onward flight within twelve hours`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `official passport`                     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Transit passenger`
`the passenger who` nationality `only in the transit area` `holds a transit visa` `exempt under Visa Code Article 3(5)` `visa and ticket for AU IL NZ` `returning to Jordan` `onward flight within twelve hours` `official passport` MEANS
    `Transit passenger` WITH
        `nationality` IS nationality
        `stays only in the international transit area` IS `only in the transit area`
        `holds an airport transit visa` IS `holds a transit visa`
        `is exempt under Visa Code Article 3(5)` IS `exempt under Visa Code Article 3(5)`
        `holds a valid visa for Australia Israel or New Zealand and a ticket or boarding pass for a flight there` IS `visa and ticket for AU IL NZ`
        `is returning to Jordan from a lawful stay in Australia Israel or New Zealand with a ticket or boarding pass` IS `returning to Jordan`
        `onward flight leaves within twelve hours of arrival from the airport whose transit area the person never leaves` IS `onward flight within twelve hours`
        `holds a service passport a ministerial passport or another passport for official travel` IS `official passport`

§ `Do I need an airport transit visa?`

@export Must I hold an airport transit visa to change planes at a German airport, reading Annex C of the Residence Regulation as it is printed? Answers yes or no from § 26(2) AufenthV.
GIVEN
    nationality                             IS A STRING  @desc The English name of the state whose passport you travel on, for example Mali, Jordan or Türkiye.
    `only in the transit area`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you stay in the international transit area of the airport and never enter Germany.
    `holds a transit visa`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you already hold an airport transit visa.
    `exempt under Visa Code Article 3(5)`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you fall within a category exempted from the visa by Article 3(5) of the EU Visa Code, such as holding a visa or residence permit issued by an EU state.
    `visa and ticket for AU IL NZ`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Jordanian nationals only: true if you hold a valid visa for Australia, Israel or New Zealand and a ticket or boarding pass for a flight to that state.
    `returning to Jordan`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Jordanian nationals only: true if you are travelling to Jordan after a lawful stay in Australia, Israel or New Zealand and hold a ticket or boarding pass to Jordan.
    `onward flight within twelve hours`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Jordanian nationals only: true if your onward flight leaves within twelve hours of your arrival in Germany, from the airport whose transit area you never leave.
    `official passport`                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Turkish nationals only: true if you hold a service passport, a ministerial passport or another passport for travel in an official capacity or on official business.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`must I hold an airport transit visa under Annex C as printed` MEANS
    `the traveller must hold an airport transit visa under the reading`
        `as printed`
        (`the passenger who` nationality `only in the transit area` `holds a transit visa` `exempt under Visa Code Article 3(5)` `visa and ticket for AU IL NZ` `returning to Jordan` `onward flight within twelve hours` `official passport`)

@export Am I exempt from needing a residence title while I wait in the transit area of a German airport, reading Annex C as it is printed? Answers yes or no from § 26(1) and (2) sentence 2 AufenthV.
GIVEN
    nationality                             IS A STRING  @desc The English name of the state whose passport you travel on, for example Mali, Jordan or Türkiye.
    `only in the transit area`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you stay in the international transit area of the airport and never enter Germany.
    `holds a transit visa`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you already hold an airport transit visa.
    `exempt under Visa Code Article 3(5)`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you fall within a category exempted from the visa by Article 3(5) of the EU Visa Code, such as holding a visa or residence permit issued by an EU state.
    `visa and ticket for AU IL NZ`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Jordanian nationals only: true if you hold a valid visa for Australia, Israel or New Zealand and a ticket or boarding pass for a flight to that state.
    `returning to Jordan`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Jordanian nationals only: true if you are travelling to Jordan after a lawful stay in Australia, Israel or New Zealand and hold a ticket or boarding pass to Jordan.
    `onward flight within twelve hours`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Jordanian nationals only: true if your onward flight leaves within twelve hours of your arrival in Germany, from the airport whose transit area you never leave.
    `official passport`                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Turkish nationals only: true if you hold a service passport, a ministerial passport or another passport for travel in an official capacity or on official business.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`am I exempt from the residence title requirement in transit under Annex C as printed` MEANS
    `the traveller is exempt from the residence-title requirement under the reading`
        `as printed`
        (`the passenger who` nationality `only in the transit area` `holds a transit visa` `exempt under Visa Code Article 3(5)` `visa and ticket for AU IL NZ` `returning to Jordan` `onward flight within twelve hours` `official passport`)

-- The next group only arises if your state's entry in Annex C was added by the 2015 amending regulation (the article names Mali and South Sudan).
-- A form can ask "Is your state Mali or South Sudan?" before showing it.
§ `What if the 2015 additions to Annex C are void?`

@export Must I hold an airport transit visa to change planes at a German airport, if the 2015 amendment of Annex C (Mali in place of Myanmar, South Sudan added) is void because the amending regulation did not cite § 99(3a) of the Residence Act? Answers yes or no.
GIVEN
    nationality                             IS A STRING  @desc The English name of the state whose passport you travel on, for example Mali, South Sudan or Jordan.
    `only in the transit area`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you stay in the international transit area of the airport and never enter Germany.
    `holds a transit visa`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you already hold an airport transit visa.
    `exempt under Visa Code Article 3(5)`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you fall within a category exempted from the visa by Article 3(5) of the EU Visa Code.
    `visa and ticket for AU IL NZ`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Jordanian nationals only: true if you hold a valid visa for Australia, Israel or New Zealand and a ticket or boarding pass for a flight to that state.
    `returning to Jordan`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Jordanian nationals only: true if you are travelling to Jordan after a lawful stay in Australia, Israel or New Zealand and hold a ticket or boarding pass to Jordan.
    `onward flight within twelve hours`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Jordanian nationals only: true if your onward flight leaves within twelve hours of your arrival in Germany from the airport whose transit area you never leave.
    `official passport`                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Turkish nationals only: true if you hold a service passport, a ministerial passport or another passport for travel in an official capacity or on official business.
    `an exception applies`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether to assume that an exception to the citation requirement applies, so that the 2015 additions stand: false assumes none applies and the additions are void.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`must I hold an airport transit visa if the 2015 amendment is void` MEANS
    `the traveller must hold an airport transit visa under the reading`
        (`the reading of Annex C to apply` `an exception applies`)
        (`the passenger who` nationality `only in the transit area` `holds a transit visa` `exempt under Visa Code Article 3(5)` `visa and ticket for AU IL NZ` `returning to Jordan` `onward flight within twelve hours` `official passport`)

@export Am I exempt from needing a residence title while I wait in the transit area of a German airport, if the 2015 amendment of Annex C (Mali in place of Myanmar, South Sudan added) is void because the amending regulation did not cite § 99(3a) of the Residence Act? Answers yes or no.
GIVEN
    nationality                             IS A STRING  @desc The English name of the state whose passport you travel on, for example Mali, South Sudan or Jordan.
    `only in the transit area`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you stay in the international transit area of the airport and never enter Germany.
    `holds a transit visa`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you already hold an airport transit visa.
    `exempt under Visa Code Article 3(5)`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you fall within a category exempted from the visa by Article 3(5) of the EU Visa Code.
    `visa and ticket for AU IL NZ`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Jordanian nationals only: true if you hold a valid visa for Australia, Israel or New Zealand and a ticket or boarding pass for a flight to that state.
    `returning to Jordan`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Jordanian nationals only: true if you are travelling to Jordan after a lawful stay in Australia, Israel or New Zealand and hold a ticket or boarding pass to Jordan.
    `onward flight within twelve hours`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Jordanian nationals only: true if your onward flight leaves within twelve hours of your arrival in Germany from the airport whose transit area you never leave.
    `official passport`                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Turkish nationals only: true if you hold a service passport, a ministerial passport or another passport for travel in an official capacity or on official business.
    `an exception applies`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether to assume that an exception to the citation requirement applies, so that the 2015 additions stand: false assumes none applies and the additions are void.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`am I exempt from the residence title requirement in transit if the 2015 amendment is void` MEANS
    `the traveller is exempt from the residence-title requirement under the reading`
        (`the reading of Annex C to apply` `an exception applies`)
        (`the passenger who` nationality `only in the transit area` `holds a transit visa` `exempt under Visa Code Article 3(5)` `visa and ticket for AU IL NZ` `returning to Jordan` `onward flight within twelve hours` `official passport`)

@export Does the preamble of the 2015 regulation that amended the Residence Regulation cite § 99(3a) of the Residence Act, the power to name the states whose nationals need an airport transit visa? Answers yes or no, on the article's quotation of that preamble.
`does the 2015 preamble cite the power to add a state to Annex C` MEANS
    `the preamble cites the power`
        `the power needed to add a state to Annex C`
        `the powers cited in the preamble of the 2015 amending regulation`
